            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> (drive-by comment, ignore if irrelevant:)\r\n> \r\n> rather than \"expose\", I would expect that we actually just _use extmarks_ to implement OSC 8 in terminal. (and thus, there should be lots of _deleted_ code in this PR, too.) may be (conceptually) related to: #7406\r\n> \r\n> cc @gpanders\r\n\r\nThere would not be lots of deleted code because the implementation in `terminal.c` was always pretty minimal, it \"just\" sets the `url` highlight attribute and lets the highlight engine do the rest of the work.\r\n\r\nUsing extmarks here is kind of a hack, we're not using extmarks to highlight terminal buffers in any other way, so we're throwing extmarks on top just so that we can retrieve the URL metadata. I still think my 2nd option in the linked solution is the better approach:\r\n\r\n>Provide an API to retrieve the URL (or other attributes) from a highlight attribute ID (or from an arbitrary buffer position). Since URLs are only attached to \"anonymous\" highlight attributes (not highlight groups) this would need to be a new API.",
